I built the sprint board in `src/` (App, BoardPage, ArchivePage, plus `boardMachine.ts`, `archiveMachine.ts`, `appMachine.ts`, `ops.ts`, `requests.ts` and `model.ts`). Each user action spawns its own XState op actor that makes one server call and reports back, so optimistic edits roll back independently, and the selected card's checklist is an invoked actor that restarts on reselect. `./check` passes and all 26 visible tests pass (3 of 15 runs used); I also exercised concurrent moves, out-of-order replies, reselecting, rollbacks and retries directly against the machines under Node. Unsure points: the brief doesn't say whether the rename input empties after a rename (I left it as typed), I disabled add-item and toggle while a checklist is still loading, and a rename or item error for a card you've since left is stored but not shown.